F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/views/proposals.mjs efe31f0269d2 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context pane's Proposals queue (spec 09, VIEW-3), pure: a card per proposal with its kind and module, its text, its evidence in words, and two sparklines (spark: a bar per week over 8 weeks, its height the week's count against the busiest) of the decisions that served it (green) and overrode it (red); Ratify, Drop… and Defer (Bring back) buttons; the selected one in a bold cyan border. queueOrder puts deferred proposals after the waiting ones; queueKeys gives the selected proposal r (ratify), d (drop) and f (defer) as the frame's keys.
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/view.mjs 351765723d0a 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human What the Context Graph mod draws, as pure functions of the ctx CLI's JSON and the elements $.ui.resolve gives: followedPath (which tool calls move the pane, repo-relative), contextPane (through views/frame.mjs: the health header, tabs File, Proposals (views/proposals.mjs's queue and its r/d/f keys) and Coverage, the keys), its sections laid out as headed fixed-width labelled rows (file: path and who touched it, the card as Markdown where the surface draws it, understood with what's unread, module, rules as chips coloured by kind (enforced red, guidance blue, proposed yellow), decisions, the neighbourhood from ctx neighbours (imports and importers as buttons with a card glyph, ● current ◐ stale ○ missing, and ✗ with the rules each breaks), code-kit with Open Lanes, Write card or Update card when the card isn't current, Cards for this module; coverage as a table per agent, the selected one marked, with every edit marked understood or not), and dropPane. No mods API, files or processes, so vitest tests it.
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/register.mjs b8d9a99fef2a 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context Graph mod's hooks (Claude Code 2.1.287+): registers /graph (not /context, Claude Code's own, or /ctx, the plugin's ctx skill) and /graph-settings. /graph toggles the Context pane; /graph <path> opens it on that file and pins it there until the person follows the agents again (code-kit's combined view opens files this way). Follows the file an agent last read or edited from tool.call when not pinned (watch only, with a pass-through catch), reads the ctx CLI's JSON (info, proposals, cards, agents, file, neighbours, settings) and refreshes within 2 s of a tool call or a .ctx file change. Keeps the pane's tab, selection and back stack (VIEW-5): j/k select, Enter opens an agent's unread edit, a neighbour press opens that file (VIEW-2), the proposals the person deferred this session wait at the back of the queue (VIEW-3), and a ui.close hook makes the person's Escape go back (restoring the file it came from) before it closes. Draws the Context pane, the Drop dialog, the Settings view and a band line of the graph's health (views/frame.mjs) stacked above whatever else the band holds; runs the person's acts (ratify --commit, drop --reason --commit, settings set --reason --via pane) only from its own buttons, and asks the lead for cards as a prompt. Never enforces; never imports src.
