F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/register.mjs 6ff78b012f61 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context Graph mod's hooks (Claude Code 2.1.287+): registers /graph (not /context, Claude Code's own, or /ctx, the plugin's ctx skill) and /graph-settings. /graph toggles the Context pane; /graph <path> opens it on that file and pins it there until the person follows the agents again (code-kit's combined view opens files this way). Follows the file an agent last read or edited from tool.call when not pinned (watch only, with a pass-through catch), and there also keeps read-assist (ASSIST-1): a read-before-edit refusal is kept by its call's id, and a subagent is told what to read with $.session.send; edits that went through are kept for their card-owed tag. Reads the ctx CLI's JSON (info, proposals, cards, agents, file, neighbours, settings), refreshing each open reading list's progress from ctx file --agent (ASSIST-2), within 2 s of a tool call or a .ctx file change. Keeps the pane's tab, selection and back stack (VIEW-5): j/k select, Enter opens an agent's unread edit, a neighbour press opens that file (VIEW-2), deferred proposals wait at the back of the queue (VIEW-3), and a ui.close hook makes the person's Escape go back before it closes. Draws the Context pane, the Drop dialog, the Settings view, a band line of the graph's health (views/frame.mjs) stacked above whatever else the band holds, tool rows' tags (ToolUse, composed over what's beneath) and a refused edit's result as its reading list (ToolResult); runs the person's acts (ratify --commit, drop --reason --commit, settings set --reason --via pane) only from its own buttons, and asks the lead for cards as a prompt. Never enforces; never imports src.
