F src/cli/main.ts 1a9f010f36a7 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The ctx command line: parseArgs, the usage text, and the commands hooks and agents call often (slice, hydrate, why, history, record, card, pending, coverage, doctor, install, hook, mcp, adopt, link, embed). Rarer commands fall through to extraCommands in commands.ts so this file stays cheap to load. Exports Args, parseArgs, str, readInput, latestSession, openFromArgs and needGraph, which the lazily loaded command modules (init/cli.ts, hygiene/cli.ts, cli/module.ts, cli/settings.ts, cli/neighbours.ts and others) rely on. The usage text is what ctx help prints, so new commands and flags are listed there: it names ctx cards with --changed and --module, ctx module <L:id> --paths with --in, --name and --delegated --reason, ctx settings [set <key> <value> --reason], ctx neighbours <path>, alongside file, agents, proposals, drop, propose and ratify --commit.
F src/cli/settings.ts 01cbd29afd82 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human ctx settings: lists the [harness] settings in force with their defaults and about lines (--json for the mod; pause_at_percent also carries inForce and from when a tool sharing the repository sets the pause point itself, code-kit's winning), and settings set <key> <value> --reason [--via pane] changes one as the person's act: validated by harness.ts, written into .ctx/config.toml with withHarnessSetting (the rest of the file untouched), and recorded by any tool adapter that guards the file (code-kit's approval log). The hooks refuse settings set from every agent (person-acts.ts).
