F src/tool-adapters/code-kit.ts e9814ba3230c 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human What ctx knows about code-kit when it shares the repository: a file's spec requirements, lane and layer from code-kit trace (cached per checkout), a session-start note, the branches code-kit protects (from .claude/code-kit.json, defaulting to main and master), where a person's graph commit must not land, its pause point for background agents (harness.background.pauseAtPercent, 80 unless set), which wins over Context Graph's own, and recordPersonsChange: a harness setting the person changes in .ctx/config.toml (which code-kit protects under its approval ctx) is approved with code-kit approve ctx --reason, marked --via context-graph when made in the pane, so code-kit's log keeps it as theirs when committed.
F src/tool-adapters/index.ts 3da78c79744f 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human Tool adapters: what ctx knows about another tool sharing a repository, kept out of the core. Each is detected per checkout and may contribute file facts, a session note, protected branches, a pause point for background agents (pauseAtPercent, which wins over Context Graph's own), and a way to record a person's change to a graph file it guards (recordPersonsChange); the core only calls toolAdapters, factsFor and toolProtectedBranches and the optional methods, and never names a tool.
