F src/hygiene/hygiene.ts d6c75903d8b4 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human Hygiene and evolution of the graph: hygieneReport proposes from evidence (rules overridden in practice on a streak, agreed rules overridden overrideStreak or more times since they were ratified (overridden-since-ratified, CUR-2, reported once when the streak also holds), unreachable attachments, dormant modules, missing tests, deleted paths, orphaned bases, expired proposals, superseded ADRs, pack mapping drift, debt trend) and never retires; gc archives only what is already inactive and drops expired proposed edges; timeline merges the archive into a node's history. retire appends a Z record with a reason and takes { delegated }: the project's delegated ratifier retires under '<ratifier>/delegated', refused when no [delegate] is set, and, when the target needs ratifying (a concept or an enforced rule), refused unless may_ratify includes retirements; the trailer names '<ratifier> (delegated)'. It is used by hygiene/cli.ts, main.ts (history --timeline), cli/guide.ts, cli/present.ts, overlay/server.ts and the mod (ctx hygiene --json for the flagged rules).
