F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/why.mjs 1539db11815a 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human Side questions (spec 07), pure: targetsOf picks the graph nodes a question names (module ids, rule ids, paths; at most five); sourcesOf turns ctx why --json results into the records an answer may rest on (cards, rules and proposed rules, decisions, once each); whyPrompt asks for an answer from those records only, citing ids, and to say the graph holds nothing rather than guess (ASKQ-3); costText words the answer's time and tokens (ASKQ-2); whyPane draws the question, the answer as Markdown, its cost and its sources as buttons, beside the conversation (WHY_ID).
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/view.mjs 5c6b9a77191a 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human What the Context Graph mod draws, as pure functions of the ctx CLI's JSON and the elements $.ui.resolve gives: followedPath (which tool calls move the pane, repo-relative), contextPane (through views/frame.mjs: the health header, tabs File, Proposals (views/proposals.mjs's queue and its r/d/f keys, the Overridden rules, the curator's line with Curate now) and Coverage (the card writer's line first), the keys), its sections laid out as headed fixed-width labelled rows (file: path with Why? on w, who touched it, the card as Markdown where the surface draws it, understood with what's unread, module, rules as chips coloured by kind, decisions, the neighbourhood with card glyphs and broken rules, code-kit with Open Lanes, Write card or Update card, Cards for this module; coverage as a table per agent with every edit marked understood or not and each open reading list's progress), and dropPane. No mods API, files or processes, so vitest tests it.
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/register.mjs 99c8449420e3 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context Graph mod's hooks (Claude Code 2.1.287+): registers /graph, /why and /graph-settings, and the card writer's and curator's agents (re-registered when their model settings change). /graph toggles the Context pane; /graph <path> opens it on that file, pinned. /why (or Why? on the file in view) asks a side question: the nodes it names are looked up with ctx why, and with records found, a side call answers from them only, over the session's own context ($.model.fork, sharing the prompt cache) or the side_questions_model set ($.model.complete), in its own pane with its time, tokens and sources; with none, it says the graph holds nothing and makes no call; the lead's conversation gains nothing. Follows the file an agent last read or edited, keeps read-assist and edits, reads the ctx CLI's JSON (info, proposals, hygiene, cards, agents, file, neighbours, settings) within 2 s of a change. When the lead's turn ends, one background agent may start below the pause point: the card writer's batch, else the curator. Keeps the pane's tab, selection and back stack; Escape goes back before it closes. Draws the Context pane, the Drop dialog, the Settings view, the Why pane, the band's health line, tool rows' tags and a refused edit's reading list; runs the person's acts only from its own buttons. Never enforces; never imports src.
