F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/views/map.mjs 94eca19c8239 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context pane's Map tab (spec 08), pure: HEAT gives each file cell's state a glyph, colour and words (current, stale, missing, owed this session); heatOf lets owed win over the card's state; coverageBar is a module's carded share as ten cells and words; mapTree draws the modules indented by depth with rule counts, proposals marked, a 30-day decision sparkline (proposals.mjs's spark, three days a bar) and coverage, the selected one marked (MAP-1); heatMap draws a module's files as coloured cells (keyed by their Box), a legend counting each state, a Select for the pointer, and the selected file, which Enter opens (MAP-2, MAP-3).
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/views/proposals.mjs 23fb239e4333 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context pane's Proposals queue (spec 09, VIEW-3), pure: a card per proposal with its kind and module, its text, its evidence in words, and two sparklines (spark: a bar per span, a week unless told, its height the span's count against the busiest; the Map tab uses it for 30 days of decisions) of the decisions that served it (green) and overrode it (red); Ratify, Drop… and Defer (Bring back) buttons; the selected one in a bold cyan border. queueOrder puts deferred proposals after the waiting ones; queueKeys gives the selected proposal r (ratify), d (drop) and f (defer) as the frame's keys.
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/views/frame.mjs d5e9704962d8 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human Panes v2's frame for the Context pane (spec 09, VIEW-1 and VIEW-5), pure: healthOf turns ctx cards --json (fresh, stale, missing), the session's cards owed, the proposals waiting and the flagged rules into a carded share, a level (amber with anything owed, a flagged rule or under 80% carded; red with 5 owed or 3 flagged), a glyph (☀ ⛅ ⛈) and the line; bandHealth gives the band that line only while something waits or the health isn't good; frame draws the header with Settings, the notice, the tabs (File, Proposals, Coverage, Map on 1-4), the tab's body and the keys (j/k, o, Esc's words); DEFAULT_UI (with the Map tab's module), moved (nothing selected until j or k) and closeGoesBack (Escape goes back while the back stack holds somewhere).
