F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/register.mjs 2e7124079d86 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context Graph mod's hooks (Claude Code 2.1.287+): registers /graph, /why and /graph-settings, and the card writer's and curator's agents (re-registered when their model settings change). /graph toggles the Context pane; /graph <path> opens it on that file, pinned. /why answers a side question from the graph's records in a pane of its own (a fork over the session's context, or the model set), with no call when the graph holds nothing. Follows the file an agent last read or edited, keeps read-assist and edits, reads the ctx CLI's JSON (info, proposals, hygiene, cards, agents, file, neighbours, settings, and map while the Map tab shows) within 2 s of a change. When the lead's turn ends, one background agent may start below the pause point: the card writer's batch, else the curator. Keeps the pane's tab, selection, Map module and back stack (VIEW-5, MAP-3): j/k select, Enter opens an agent's unread edit, a module's heat map or a file in the File tab, a neighbour press opens that file; Escape goes back (restoring the file or module it came from) before it closes. Draws the Context pane, the Drop dialog, the Settings view, the Why pane, the band's health line, tool rows' tags and a refused edit's reading list; runs the person's acts only from its own buttons. Never enforces; never imports src.
