F src/cli/commands.ts 3cad2dddf4aa 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human Routes the lifecycle, runtime and presentation commands to modules loaded on demand through extraCommands(args, env), so the hook path never pays for them: init/ratify/pack (init/cli.ts), gate, hygiene/gc/retire (hygiene/cli.ts), serve/overlay, bench, next/cards (guide.ts), file/agents/proposals/drop (present.ts), propose (propose.ts), module (module.ts), settings (settings.ts), neighbours (neighbours.ts) and map (map.ts). main.ts calls it from its default case; each target module exports run(args, env) and returns an exit code, and extraCommands returns undefined for a command none of them owns so main can report it unknown. A new lazily loaded command needs its case here and its line in main.ts's usage text.
F src/cli/main.ts 2caf118f5f72 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The ctx command line: parseArgs, the usage text, and the commands hooks and agents call often (slice, hydrate, why, history, record, card, pending, coverage, doctor, install, hook, mcp, adopt, link, embed, info). info's JSON carries counts (decisions, rules) for the mod's curator. Rarer commands fall through to extraCommands in commands.ts so this file stays cheap to load. Exports Args, parseArgs, str, readInput, latestSession, openFromArgs and needGraph, which the lazily loaded command modules (init/cli.ts, hygiene/cli.ts, cli/module.ts, cli/settings.ts, cli/neighbours.ts, cli/map.ts and others) rely on. The usage text is what ctx help prints, so new commands and flags are listed there: it names ctx cards with --changed and --module, ctx module <L:id> --paths with --in, --name and --delegated --reason, ctx settings [set <key> <value> --reason], ctx neighbours <path>, ctx map, alongside file, agents, proposals, drop, propose and ratify --commit.
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/register.mjs c529c0fd332b 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context Graph mod's hooks (Claude Code 2.1.287+): registers /graph, /why and /graph-settings, and the card writer's and curator's agents (re-registered when their model settings change, and tried again at the next refresh while registering fails, as under claude -p before the session is bound). /graph toggles the Context pane; /graph <path> opens it on that file, pinned. /why answers a side question from the graph's records in a pane of its own (a fork over the session's context, or the model set), with no call when the graph holds nothing. Follows the file an agent last read or edited, keeps read-assist and edits, reads the ctx CLI's JSON (info, proposals, hygiene, cards, agents, file, neighbours, settings, and map while the Map tab shows) within 2 s of a change; a failing $.agent.list reads as no agents. When the lead's turn ends, one background agent may start below the pause point: the card writer's batch, else the curator. Keeps the pane's tab, selection, Map module and back stack: j/k select, Enter opens, Escape goes back before it closes. Draws the Context pane, the Drop dialog, the Settings view, the Why pane, the band's health line, tool rows' tags and a refused edit's reading list; runs the person's acts only from its own buttons. Never enforces; never imports src.
F adapters/claude-code/hooks/mod/register.test.ts 419e79a1a04a 2026-10-10 80552949+warrendeanlangeveldt/human The Context Graph mod end to end in claude plugin test (Claude Code 2.1.287+), with the ctx CLI stubbed by its JSON (info counts, hygiene, why, map, cards, neighbours, settings), the model's fork and complete, agent registration, the session's limits and measure, and turns: FILE-1 to FILE-5, RAT-1 to RAT-4, COV-1 to COV-3, VIEW-1 to VIEW-6, /graph <path>, ASSIST-1 to ASSIST-3, CARDW-1 to CARDW-5, CUR-1 to CUR-4, ASKQ-1 to ASKQ-3, MAP-1 to MAP-3, and a session with no agent list (claude -p before it mounts) still drawing the pane.
